<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<LanguageData>
    <!--
    This error is sent when an interaction requires the person causing the
    interaction to have a pawn assigned to them, but they do not.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.PawnRequired.Self>You don’t have a pawn.</TKUtils.Errors.PawnRequired.Self>

    <!-- 
     This error is sent when an interaction requires a person with an assigned
     pawn as the center of the interaction, like a proposal.
     -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.PawnRequired.Other>{ViewerName} doesn’t have a pawn.</TKUtils.Errors.PawnRequired.Other>

    <!--
    This error is sent when an interaction would cost the person causing the interaction
    more coins than they currently have available.
     -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InsufficentBalance>This interaction would cost you {RequiredAmount} coins, but you only have {Balance} coins.</TKUtils.Errors.InsufficentBalance>

    <!--
    This error is sent when an interaction requires a query, but the interaction yielded
    no results from the query.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery>No results by the name of "{Query}" could be found.</TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery>

    <!--
    This error is sent when an interaction requires a research project to be completed
    before the product specified can be purchased.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.UnfulfilledResearchPrerequisite>The research project "{ResearchName}" must be completed before "{ProductName}" will be available for purchase.</TKUtils.Errors.UnfulfilledResearchPrerequisite>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase a product that's disabled,
    which disallows them from purchasing said product by any means.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.ProductDisabled>The product "{ProductName}" is disabled, and cannot be purchased.</TKUtils.Errors.ProductDisabled>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to use an interaction that requires a
    loaded player-owned map.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoPlayerMapFound>This interaction requires a valid player-owned map to be loaded, but no such map exists.</TKUtils.Errors.NoPlayerMapFound>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to use an interaction that requires a
    loaded map.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoMapFound>This interaction requires a valid map to be loaded, but there are no loaded maps.</TKUtils.Errors.NoMapFound>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to use an interaction that requires a
    loaded game to be running. This can either be a save file loaded by the streamer
    or a brand new save to be active.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoLoadedGame>This interaction requires an active play session.</TKUtils.Errors.NoLoadedGame>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer specifies a color, either a hexadecimal code or
    a name, that doesn't exist in the mod's database or is in an invalid format.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InvalidColor>The color "{Color}" wasn’t recognized.</TKUtils.Errors.InvalidColor>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to acquire a trait that their pawn isn't
    capable of acquiring due to one or more of the pawn's genes suppressing said trait.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.TraitGeneSupressed>The trait "{TraitName}" cannot be added to your pawn as it’s suppressed by the gene "{GeneName}."</TKUtils.Errors.TraitGeneSupressed>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to relinquish a trait that their pawn
    isn't capable of relinquishing due to one or more of the pawn's genes adding the
    trait to their pawn. Traits added by genes are considered "gene locked" and
    cannot be removed until the gene that added them is removed or suppressed.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.TraitGeneLocked>The trait "{TraitName}" cannot be removed from your pawn as it’s added by the gene "{GeneName}."</TKUtils.Errors.TraitGeneLocked>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to acquire a trait that their pawn isn't
    capable of acquiring due to one of the pawn's backstories forbidding the trait.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.BackstoryRestrictedTrait>The trait "{TraitName}" cannot be added to your pawn as it’s forbidden by your backstory "{BackstoryName}."</TKUtils.Errors.BackstoryRestrictedTrait>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to acquire a trait that their pawn isn't
    capable of acquiring due to the pawn's kind forbidding the trait.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.KindRestrictedAddTrait>The trait "{TraitName}" cannot be added to your pawn as it’s forbidden by your pawn’s kind "{KindName}."</TKUtils.Errors.KindRestrictedAddTrait>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to relinquish a trait that their pawn isn't
    capable of relinquishing due to the pawn's kind spawning with the trait.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.KindRestrictedRemoveTrait>The trait "{TraitName}" cannot be removed from your pawn as it’s required by your pawn’s kind "{KindName}."</TKUtils.Errors.KindRestrictedRemoveTrait>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to acquire a trait that would put their
    pawn's total traits over the trait limit. Traits that are acquired organically
    through genetics, or traits that bypass the limit (like sexuality traits), are
    excluded from the total.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.TraitLimitReached>The maximum number of traits a pawn can have is {TraitLimit}. Traits that bypass the limit, or traits that were added by your xenotype, are excluded.</TKUtils.Errors.TraitLimitReached>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to acquire a trait that would conflict
    with another trait the pawn has. A conflict would occur when the trait cannot
    exist on a pawn with the other trait (e.g., Kind conflicts with Psychopath).
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.TraitConflict>The trait "{TraitName}" cannot be acquired as it conflicts with "{ConflictingTraitName}."</TKUtils.Errors.TraitConflict>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to acquire a trait that would conflict
    with another trait the pawn has. A conflict would occur when the trait is on the
    same "spectrum" as the trait the viewer is attempting to add (e.g., Slowpoke would
    conflict with Jogger as they're on the same spectrum).
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.TraitSpectrumConflict>The trait "{TraitName}" cannot be acquired as it’s on the same spectrum as "{OtherTraitName}."</TKUtils.Errors.TraitSpectrumConflict>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase one or more products whose total
    would be less than the minimum required order total. For instance, if a viewer attempts
    to purchase ten wood logs, each priced at two coins, the viewer would need to purchase
    three more wood logs to meet the hypothetical minimum of twenty-five coins.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.MinimumCartTotalNotReached>You must spend at least {MinimumCartTotal} coin(s) per purchase.</TKUtils.Errors.MinimumCartTotalNotReached>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase an item made of a specific material,
    but said item cannot be made of said material. For instance, if a viewer were to purchase
    a club made of slate, the purchase would be invalid as clubs cannot be made from slate.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.ItemMaterialInvalid>The item "{ItemName}" can’t be made of the material "{MaterialName}."</TKUtils.Errors.ItemMaterialInvalid>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase an item of a specific quality, but
    said item cannot have a quality associated with it. For instance, if a viewer were to
    purchase a packaged survival meal, the purchase would be invalid as packaged survival meals
    cannot have a quality associated with them.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.ItemQualityInvalid>The item "{ItemName}" can’t have a quality associated with it.</TKUtils.Errors.ItemQualityInvalid>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase an animal of a specific gender, but
    said animal cannot have a gender associated with it.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.AnimalGenderInvalid>The animal "{AnimalName}" can’t have a gender associated with it.</TKUtils.Errors.AnimalGenderInvalid>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase a "gender swap" on a pawn whose kind
    doesn't support genders. In RimWorld, pawns can either be "Male," "Female," or "None." It's
    pawns that are "None" that will cause this error to appear should a viewer attempt to swap
    their pawn's gender.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.GenderlessSwap>The pawn kind "{PawnKindName}" can’t have genders, so you can’t swap your gender.</TKUtils.Errors.GenderlessSwap>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase an inspiration, either random or targeted,
    but the ultimate target of the inspiration could not be inspired. This could be caused by several
    things, like the pawn being incapable of inspirations, incapable of all skills, or by all pawns
    being dead. Importantly, the underlying reason behind the failed attempt is unknown to the mod;
    for more information about inspirations, or the lack thereof, refer to the game's wiki.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InspirationYieldedNone>No pawns could be inspired at the moment. Try again later.</TKUtils.Errors.InspirationYieldedNone>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase a surgery on their pawn on the same body
    part, and the same item being surgically attached. For instance, if a viewer were to purchase 
    the surgery "Install bionic arm (left)," which is a bionic arm that replaces the pawn's left
    arm, queuing another bionic arm on the left arm would result in this error.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.SimilarSurgeryQueued>A similar surgery on your pawn’s "{BodyPartName}" is already queued.</TKUtils.Errors.SimilarSurgeryQueued>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase a surgery on their pawn, but the item
    they requested cannot be installed on the pawn. This is due to the item having no valid body
    part it can replace, like a bionic wing cannot be installed on pawns without wings. Likewise,
    the wings cannot be installed on pawns that don't have mod support that allows wings to be
    installed on pawns that normally can't have wings.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoSurgerySlot>The item "{ItemName}" can only be installed on the body part "{BodyPartName}," which your pawn doesn’t have..</TKUtils.Errors.NoSurgerySlot>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase a surgery on an item that has no valid
    surgery associated with it. For example, attempting to surgically attach a long sword will
    result in this error since there isn't a surgery in-game for attaching a long sword to a pawn.
    Should a mod be added that adds support for such a thing, then this error wouldn't occur.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InvalidSurgeryCandidate>The item "{ItemName}" can’t be surgically attached.</TKUtils.Errors.InvalidSurgeryCandidate>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase an item that can't be used by a pawn
    normally. This is typically raised for items that have no associated `Comp_Usable` or
    `Comp_Ingestable` associated with it.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.Unusable>The item "{ItemName}" can’t be used by your pawn.</TKUtils.Errors.Unusable>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase a passion shuffle, but their pawn
    doesn't have any passions.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoPassions>Your pawn doesn’t have passions that can be shuffled.</TKUtils.Errors.NoPassions>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase a trait removal, but their pawn
    doesn't have any traits can be removed. This can be either because their pawn doesn't
    have any traits, or because the traits the pawn has been forced to be there due to the
    pawn's xenotype, pawn kind, backstory, or some undisclosed reason.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoTraitsForRemoval>Your pawn doesn’t have traits that can be removed.</TKUtils.Errors.NoTraitsForRemoval>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase a trait removal, but their pawn
    doesn't have the trait they're trying to remove.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoTraitFoundForRemoval>Your pawn doesn’t have the trait "{TraitName}."</TKUtils.Errors.NoTraitFoundForRemoval>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to replace a trait on their pawn that
    currently bypasses the trait limit, like a sexuality trait. Replacing the trait
    with the viewer's requested trait, which doesn't bypass the trait limit, would
    allow the viewer to have more traits than they'd be capable of having.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.TraitReplaceWouldBypassLimit>Your pawn has the trait "{TraitName}," which bypasses the trait limit. Replacing it with "{ReplacementTraitName}" would’ve exceeded the trait limit of {TraitLimit} traits.</TKUtils.Errors.TraitReplaceWouldBypassLimit>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase one or more items that caused the
    mod to overflow when calculating the price the viewer would have to pay.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.Overflowed>The number of coins you would’ve been charged exceeded the mod’s limits. Break it into small purchases, or purchase a smaller quantity.</TKUtils.Errors.Overflowed>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to purchase either a new colonist or an event
    that would pawn a new colonist.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.ViewerAlreadyHasPawn>You're not allowed to have more than one assigned colonist.</TKUtils.Errors.ViewerAlreadyHasPawn>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to leave the colony through the leave command or
    and event that would cause their pawn to leave the colony. This safety check that causes
    this error exists to ensure viewers can't cause a caravan to be lost if their pawn were to
    leave while they're the only healthy colonist in said caravan.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.CannotLeaveWhileInCaravan>You're not allowed to leave the colony while you’re in a caravan.</TKUtils.Errors.CannotLeaveWhileInCaravan>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query information about their pawn's relationships,
    but their pawn doesn't have any significant relationships with any other colonist. Significant
    relationships are internally defined as a type of "Def" called "RelationDef." RelationDefs
    define a significant relationship a viewer may have with another colonist, such as spouses, lovers,
    or bitter rivals. Insignificant relationships are relationships inferred through logic within
    RimWorld, such as "Acquaintance" or "Friend." These insignificant relationships aren't
     concrete and rely on underlying logic that could be changed at any point.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoRelationships>Your pawn doesn’t have any significant relationships with any other colonist.</TKUtils.Errors.NoRelationships>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query information about their pawn's health,
    specifically about a certain "health capacity." Health capacities are categories of health
    the game keeps track of and are unique amongst the pawn's underlying kind, and potentially
    xenotype.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.IncapableOfCapacity>Your pawn doesn’t have the health capacity for "{CapacityName}."</TKUtils.Errors.IncapableOfCapacity>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query information about their pawn's needs,
    but their pawn doesn't have any needs.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoPawnNeeds>Your pawn doesn’t have any needs.</TKUtils.Errors.NoPawnNeeds>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query information about the pawn's work
    schedule, but their pawn is incapable of doing any work.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoPawnWork>Your pawn can’t do any work.</TKUtils.Errors.NoPawnWork>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query information about a research project,
    but no research project matches the query given.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery.ResearchProject>No research project by the name of "{Query}" could be found.</TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery.ResearchProject>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query an item, but no item matches the
    query given.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery.Item>No item by the name of "{Query}" could be found.</TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery.Item>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query a skill, but no skill matches the
    query given.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery.Skill>No skill by the name of "{Query}" could be found.</TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery.Skill>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query a pawn kind, but no kind matches 
    the query given.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery.Kind>No kind by the name of "{Query}" could be found.</TKUtils.Errors.InvalidQuery.Kind>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query a viewer, but no viewer matches
    the query given.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Error.InvalidQuery.Viewer>No viewer by the name of "{Query}" could be found.</TKUtils.Error.InvalidQuery.Viewer>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query information about the colony's research
    endeavors, but the colony isn't actively researching anything.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NotResearching>The colony isn’t researching anything at the moment.</TKUtils.Errors.NotResearching>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to marry another pawn, but either the viewer's
    pawn or their betrothed's pawn believes the marriage is a violation of what their belief
    system.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.MarriageForbiddenByBeliefs>This marriage would violate the beliefs of {ViewerName}’s pawn.</TKUtils.Errors.MarriageForbiddenByBeliefs>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to use an interaction that requires the game to
    be unpaused. While the game is paused, the interaction may momentarily halt execution until
    the game is resumed.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.GamePaused>This interaction can’t be performed while the game is paused. If the game isn’t paused, consider using the unstick command.</TKUtils.Errors.GamePaused>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to heal their pawn of a condition, but the pawn
    doesn't have any conditions that can be healed. This can be either because the pawn doesn't
    have any conditions, at all, or because the pawn only has conditions the mod isn't capable
    of adequately healing.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NotInjured>Your pawn either isn’t injured, or has no conditions that can be healed.</TKUtils.Errors.NotInjured>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to use an interaction that requires the viewer to
    wager a certain number of coins. However, the viewer either didn't wager enough coins or never
    wagered any coins in the first place.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.WagerRequired>This interaction requires a wager anywhere between {MinimumWagerAmount} coins and {MaximumWagerAmount} coins.</TKUtils.Errors.WagerRequired>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to use an interaction that doesn't allow the viewer's
    pawn to be in combat. This combat check typically has a grace period of a couple of hours after 
    the fight is through.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.PawnInCombat>This interaction can’t be performed while in combat. Try again later.</TKUtils.Errors.PawnInCombat>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to query, or otherwise set, their work priorities, but
    the viewer is incapable of work.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.IncapableOfWork>Your pawn is completely incapable of working,.</TKUtils.Errors.IncapableOfWork>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to divorce a viewer's pawn, but the viewer initiating
    the divorce doesn't have any spouses.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NoSpouses>Your pawn isn’t married to anyone.</TKUtils.Errors.NoSpouses>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to divorce another viewer, but neither viewer is
    married to one another.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NotMarried.Other>Your pawn isn’t married to {ViewerName}.</TKUtils.Errors.NotMarried.Other>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to revive themselves, but their
    pawn isn't dead.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NotDead.Self>Your pawn isn’t dead, so you can’t revive yourself.</TKUtils.Errors.NotDead.Self>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to revive another viewer,
    but the other viewer's pawn isn't dead.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NotDead.Other>The requested pawn isn’t dead, so you can’t revive them.</TKUtils.Errors.NotDead.Other>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to revive a random pawn,
    but there aren't any dead pawns to revive.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.NotDead.Random>Everyone's alive, so you can’t revive anyone.</TKUtils.Errors.NotDead.Random>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to perform an action on a pawn, but
    said pawn is being garbage collected.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.DiscardedPawn>The pawn is being removed.</TKUtils.Errors.DiscardedPawn>

    <!--
    This error is sent when a viewer attempts to revive an unnatural corpse, which
    cannot be revived, period.
    -->
    <TKUtils.Errors.UnnaturalCorpseResurrection>No number of coins nor lengthy incantations will resurrect this void-sent.</TKUtils.Errors.UnnaturalCorpseResurrection>
</LanguageData>
